{"schema_version":"1.0.0","metadata":{"trial_id":"202610080659-shophouse","prompting_method_id":"concept-build-free.v0","model_id":"claude-opus-5-5","seed":11,"server_state_id":"concept-free.v1"},"style":{"name":"Market Shophouse: Bakery & Potions — stone-footed, timber-jettied merchant house","rationale":"Stone carries the load and wood shapes the building, with green as the one note of colour. The ground floor is stone_bricks, split into two shops by corner piers and a 2-wide central pier. Each shopfront is recessed 1 block by leaving out the front plane: the glass, stallriser and door sit at z=1, and the bakery's barrels and hay and the apothecary's brewing stand and bottles show through the glass. The ochre-plaster upper storey (smooth_sandstone) is jettied 1 block over the street on an oak floor-beam course, carried by upside-down oak-stair corbels at every pier. Lanterns hang beneath and spruce-slab awnings project to the +2 plane. Oak posts stack over the piers. Each bay has a 2x2 window set back into a reveal, with green_terracotta shutters, pots on the sill and a trapdoor box front. The gable roof's ridge runs along the street at y16, with eaves overhanging to z=-2 and z=12, a stone-brick slab cornice tucked under each eave and stone_brick_stairs verges stepping up both gables. The timber-framed gable ends have a collar beam at y12, a king post and small windows. A stone chimney over the bakery oven rises through the back slope to campfire smoke. A cobble-and-stone sidewalk carries planters and hanging lanterns."},"palette":{"manifest":["minecraft:stone_bricks","minecraft:cobblestone","minecraft:smooth_sandstone","minecraft:oak_log","minecraft:spruce_stairs","minecraft:spruce_slab","minecraft:spruce_planks","minecraft:stone_brick_stairs","minecraft:stone_brick_slab","minecraft:green_terracotta","minecraft:oak_stairs","minecraft:glass_pane","minecraft:spruce_door","minecraft:spruce_trapdoor","minecraft:potted_poppy","minecraft:potted_allium","minecraft:potte